[496.678673, "o", "Done. Both implementations are built, installed, and verified.\r\n\r\n## Deliverables in `/app`\r\n\r\n| File | Purpose |\r\n|---|---|\r\n| `serial.c` | Serial de Bruijn graph implementation |\r\n| `pgen.upc` | Parallel Berkeley UPC implementation |\r\n| `serial` | Serial executable |\r\n| `pgen` | Parallel UPC executable |\r\n| `Makefile` | Builds both (`make`, plus `make check`) |\r\n| `serial.out` | Serial contigs |\r\n| `pgen_0.out … pgen_3.out` | Parallel contigs (one file per UPC thread) |\r\n| `README.md` | Design/build/run documentation |\r\n\r\n## Results\r\n\r\n`serial` found **6 contigs** covering all 10,000 k-mers exactly (sum of contig lengths = 6·19 + 9,994 = 10,108). The parallel version produced the identical contig set:\r\n\r\n```\r\nIDENTICAL contig sets\r\n```\r\n\r\nContig lengths: `3598, 1467, 846, 380, 3590, 227` bp.\r\n\r\n## Algorithm\r\n\r\n- Graph vertices are unique k-mers; edge `u → v` when `v = u[1:] + right_ext(u)`.\r\n- Hash table with separate chaining.\r\n- Since each k-mer has at most one left and one right extension, the graph is disjoint simple paths plus simple cycles. Contigs are maximal paths starting at in-degree-0 vertices; cycles are emitted deterministically.\r\n- Parallel version: thread 0 scatters input into shared arrays; all threads insert into a shared hash table protected by striped UPC locks; each thread computes edges and traverses its own stripe of start vertices, writing to `/app/pgen_<thread>.out`. Cycles are emitted deterministically by thread 0 after a barrier so output matches serial exactly.\r\n\r\n## Verification performed\r\n\r\n- Provided `/app/test` with 1, 2, 3, 4, and 8 threads — all match serial.\r\n- Synthetic tests: true cycles, self-loops, isolated k-mers, k=1, CRLF input, duplicate k-mers, multiple genomes, shuffled input, and a 20,000-k-mer input — all match across every thread count.\r\n\r\nBuild/run:\r\n\r\n```bash\r\ncd /app && make\r\n./serial test\r\nupcrun -n 4 -shared-heap 256MB /app/pgen test\r\nmake check        # compares sorted contig sets\r\n```\r\n\r\nAs expected for this small dataset, the parallel version is slower (≈1.06 s vs <0.01 s) due to UPC startup, thread synchronization, and shared-memory access overhead.\r\n"]
